        {
          "id": "90ae4245-d80f-30fa-b54a-f7deed19d491",
          "content": {
            "id": "90ae4245-d80f-30fa-b54a-f7deed19d491",
            "contentType": "STORY",
            "title": "How The 'First Sale Rule' Is Helping Many Businesses Work Around Tariff Costs",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "U.S. companies are using a 1988 customs law called the \"first sale rule\" to get around new tariffs The law allows importers to use the price of the first sale in a series of transactions rather than its import price to calculate potential levies Mocler and Traeger are among the companies that have openly discussed implementing the law to lower tariff impacts A decades-old piece of legislation is helping many businesses mitigate the worst effects of the tariffs, CNBC reports. Part of U.S. customs",
